# a sin said plainly, the count a run ends on, where its checklist is, a warning, and a run that ended early
^(?:\S+, line \d+:|\d+ sins? across \d+ skills?\.$|\d+ sins? in \d+ files?$|[✓✗⚠] |↳ checklist written to )
progress: ^(?:parsing|reading|detector) (\d+)/(\d+)$
label: Judging the project against its commandments
commands: commandments(-release|-go)? judge
finished: ^(?:\d+ sins? across \d+ skills?\.$|\d+ sins? in \d+ files?$|✓ |↳ checklist written to )
failed: ^(?:✗ )
summary: ^(\d+ sins? across \d+ skills?\.|\d+ sins? in \d+ files?|✓ .+|✗ .+)$
